## Spec-Driven Workflow

This project uses the cpf plugin's `/cpf:specforge` skill. Run the steps
in order; each stops if a prerequisite artifact is missing.

| Step | Command                       | Artifact          | Status   |
| ---- | ----------------------------- | ----------------- | -------- |
| 1    | `/cpf:specforge constitution` | constitution.md   | [STATUS] |
| 2    | `/cpf:specforge spec`         | spec.md           | [STATUS] |
| 3    | `/cpf:specforge clarify`      | spec.md (updated) | [STATUS] |
| 4    | `/cpf:specforge plan`         | plan.md           | [STATUS] |
| 5    | `/cpf:specforge features`     | feature_list.json | [STATUS] |
| 6    | `/cpf:specforge analyze`      | readiness score   | [STATUS] |

`/cpf:specforge setup` (optional, after `plan`) prints a setup
checklist. `/cpf:specforge help` lists all sub-commands. The workflow
document, prompts, spec templates, and CI principles are provided by
the plugin; to customize one, place a copy at `.cpf/overrides/<path>`.

## Subagent Delegation (customize)

- **Delegate:** changes spanning 3+ files, security-sensitive fixes,
  full test suite runs, large refactors
- **Run in parallel:** independent analyses; lint, test, and type-check
  runs; reviews of separate modules
- **Keep in the main conversation:** orchestration, user questions,
  quick single-file edits, plan updates

## Quality Checks

cpf enforces its checks through these hooks. The lint, project, and
commit-message checks live in `.cpf/runtime/` (`verify.sh`,
`commit-check.sh`), shared with CI.

| Hook           | Trigger               | Action                                                                                                     |
| -------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| protect-files  | Before Write/Edit     | Block edits to keys, credentials, `.env`, lock files                                                       |
| validate-bash  | Before Bash           | Block destructive commands (`rm -rf /`, force push, `reset --hard`)                                        |
| validate-pr    | Before `gh pr create` | Apply commit/PR rules to title and description                                                             |
| post-edit      | After Write/Edit      | Format the edited file                                                                                     |
| format-changed | Stop                  | Format all changed files                                                                                   |
| verify-quality | Stop                  | `verify.sh --boundary agent`: linters plus the orchestrator in `.cpf/policy.json`; failure blocks the stop |
| check-upgrade  | Prompt submit         | Notice when the plugin is newer than the project                                                           |
| pre-commit     | `git commit`          | Block `main`, forbidden files, secrets; `verify.sh --boundary git --staged`                                |
| commit-msg     | `git commit`          | `commit-check.sh` on the message                                                                           |
| [HOOK_NAME]    | [TRIGGER]             | [PURPOSE]                                                                                                  |

Install or reinstall the git hooks with `.cpf/scripts/install-hooks.sh`;
check prerequisites with `/cpf:specforge doctor`.

### cpf Files

- `.cpf/policy.json` -- project-owned: per-tool include/exclude globs
  and severity, verify-quality orchestrator (`none`, `task`, `custom`)
- `.cpf/runtime/`, `.cpf/scripts/` -- managed by cpf; do not edit
- `.cpf/overrides/` -- project copies of plugin-provided files
- `.cpf/upstream-cache/` -- baselines upgrade uses to detect local edits
- `.cpf/pending/` -- upstream versions of managed files you edited
  locally; merge by hand, then delete
- `.prettierignore`, `.markdownlint-cli2.yaml` (`ignores` list), and
  `.cpf/shellcheck-excludes.txt` are generated from the policy

After updating the plugin, run `/cpf:specforge upgrade`.

## Git Commit Guidelines

- Never commit to `main`; create a feature branch from `origin/main`.
  `CPF_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1` is for release automation and the first
  commit of a new repository only.
- Conventional Commits:
  `feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|perf|test|build|ci|chore|revert`
- Subject <= 72 characters; the PR title must also leave room for the
  " (#N)" suffix
- No emoji, AI-isms, self-references, marketing adjectives, or
  `Co-Authored-By` trailers
- Make atomic commits and push them unsquashed; squash happens at merge

### PR Workflow

Before each commit, check that the branch's PR is not merged
(`gh pr view` or `glab mr view`); if it is, start a new branch from
`origin/main`. Before opening a PR, `git fetch origin`,
`git rebase origin/main`, and confirm CI passes; the diff must contain
only this branch's work.

## Error Handling

When a command fails, report the error and diagnose the root cause
before acting further. Do not silently retry or split a failing command.

## Communication Style

Technical, direct, terse. No emoji, no AI-isms ("I have", "Certainly"),
no marketing adjectives ("seamless", "robust", "elegant").
